{"seconds": 41.2, "exit": 0, "final": "After e6, Black can play fxe6+ with check. That's not as clean. Bf8+ is clearly superior since it forces mate in 2.\n\n**Best move: Bf8+**\n\n**Main line:** Bf8+ Kg6 h5#\n\n**Motif:** mate (or back-rank mate pattern, though technically the king isn't on the back rank)\n\n**Explanation:**\nBf8+ forces the Black king to g6 (only legal move, as it's in check). Then h5 is checkmate\u2014the pawns on g5 and h5 trap the king on g6, with the bishop on f8 controlling the f6 escape square. The lesson: when your opponent's king is exposed and crowded by pawns, a forcing sequence with checks can lead to instant mate.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bf8+\", \"line\": [\"Bf8+\", \"Kg6\", \"h5#\"], \"motifs\": [\"mate\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/p3Bp1p/7k/1p1KP1p1/6PP/8/3b4/8 w - - 0 44"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/p3Bp1p/7k/1p1KP1p1/6PP/8/3b4/8 w - - 0 44"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/p3Bp1p/7k/1p1KP1p1/6PP/8/3b4/8 w - - 0 44"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/p3Bp1p/7k/1p1KP1p1/6PP/8/3b4/8 w - - 0 44", "move": "Bxg5+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/p4p1p/7k/1p1KP1B1/6PP/8/3b4/8 b - - 0 44", "move": "Bxg5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/p4p1p/7k/1p1KP1B1/6PP/8/3b4/8 b - - 0 44", "move": "Kg7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/p4pkp/8/1p1KP1B1/6PP/8/3b4/8 w - - 1 45", "move": "Bh6+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/p3Bp1p/7k/1p1KP1p1/6PP/8/3b4/8 w - - 0 44", "move": "hxg5+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/p3Bp1p/7k/1p1KP1P1/6P1/8/3b4/8 b - - 0 44", "move": "Bxg5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/p3Bp1p/7k/1p1KP1P1/6P1/8/3b4/8 b - - 0 44", "move": "Kg6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/p3Bp1p/7k/1p1KP